{"items": [{"owner": {"account_id": 7565436, "reputation": 1289, "user_id": 5741227, "user_type": "registered", "accept_rate": 86, "profile_image": "https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/1d13cf5faeab09d5f2f41222a9ecf3e9?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG", "display_name": "iamjoshua", "link": "https://stackoverflow.com/users/5741227/iamjoshua"}, "is_accepted": true, "score": 2, "last_activity_date": 1579234882, "last_edit_date": 1579234882, "creation_date": 1579223305, "answer_id": 59779932, "question_id": 59607032, "content_license": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "body": "<p>The Solution for me was removing </p>\n\n<pre><code>&lt;PurgeChildEntries&gt;true&lt;/PurgeChildEntries&gt; \n</code></pre>\n\n<p>in my Invalidate Cache Policy as for some reason it randomly invalidates caches that is not inputted in the reference of a  property. Hence the intermittent response being receive in the Lookup Cache Policy.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://community.apigee.com/questions/78168/lookupcachelookupcachepolicycachehit-shows-either.html?childToView=78472#answer-78472\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">See this link for further details</a></p>\n"}], "has_more": false, "quota_max": 300, "quota_remaining": 286}